  (text "ANALOG MICS -> ADAU1860 ADC0/1/2        LIMA 2026-09-09   lima:docs/h1-headset-mute-relay.md\n\nCHANNEL BUDGET IS NOW FULL. The ADAU1860 has exactly THREE ADCs (AINP/N 0,1,2;\n  datasheet: \"three ADC channels and one DAC channel\"). Three mics uses all of\n  them, ZERO spare. Nothing else analog can be added without changing part.\n\nALL THREE MICS ARE ON THE AERONODE SIDE. They are our mics, biased from our rail\n  and referenced to our GND, so they never touch AC_GND. The isolation boundary\n  on audio-mute.kicad_sch is untouched - no transformer is needed here.\n\nFRONT END, per channel: Rn (100R) + Cn (1uF) filter the supply at the connector.\n  C2n / C3n couple OUT and the mic's local GND into AINPn / AINNn - pseudo-\n  differential, so cable ground noise is rejected. This mirrors the EVB, which\n  puts 22uF in series with BOTH legs and no bias network (UG-2017 Figure 8).\n\nUSE AMPLIFIED MIC MODULES, NOT BARE CAPSULES.\n  The ADAU1860 has NO MICBIAS pin, and its PGA is only 0-24 dB against a 0.49\n  Vrms single-ended full scale. A bare electret gives a few mV: x16 lands about\n  -24 dBFS at best and the rest has to come from digital gain, which lifts the\n  noise floor with it. Modules must output a few hundred mV and run off 3V3_MIC.\n\n3V3_MIC MUST BE ITS OWN QUIET RAIL - not the CM5's 3V3. ANC noise performance is\n  set by the mic supply. [gap] No LDO is specified yet, which is why 3V3_MIC\n  shows one deliberate \"label not connected\" ERC error on the parent sheet.\n\nANC - ONE ARCHITECTURAL BLOCKER, and it is NOT on this sheet:\n  K1 is a CHANGEOVER, so the DAC only reaches the earcup while K1 is energised.\n  ANC anti-noise has to be permanently connected. Either K1 sums instead of\n  switching, or the ANC output needs its own always-on path. See section 19.\n  T1 is NOT a blocker - I first read its 200 Hz-4 kHz spec band as a hard limit,\n  but that is Bourns' 600R telecom condition. Into 160R from a low-Z drive the\n  calculated corner is 3.4 Hz (-0.02 dB at 50 Hz). [gap] LF distortion unmeasured.\n  LATENCY: at 48 kHz the ADC->DSP->DAC loop is ~1 ms, too slow for feedforward\n  above a few hundred Hz. Run ANC through FastDSP at a high rate - the datasheet\n  characterises it at 768 kHz for exactly this."
    (at 195 85 0)
    (effects (font (size 1 1)))
    (uuid "98f6d9b0-b769-4201-bf39-f360abc96732")
  )
